{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '338,357p' Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '9840,9902p' Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js && rg -n 'SHELL_CSS|esh-ttl|esh-hb|esh-mod|esh-obj|esh-vit' Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n- `input.screen`: the game's screen (mouse positions are read through it)\n- `input.steer = 'stick'` †: 'stick' (a stick drawn under the thumb) or 'drag' (a finger anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows the thumb)\n- `input.stick = [0, 0]` †: the touch stick's direction [x, y], length <= 1\n- `input.stickDeadzone = .12` †: the part of that radius a thumb moves before the stick counts (0..0.5)\n- `input.stickId` †: the pointer (finger) holding the touch stick\n- `input.stickOn = false` †: a finger is on it\n- `input.stickRadius = 44` †: how far (CSS pixels) a finger drags for full tilt\n- `input.stickSide = 'left'` †: 'left' or 'right', the half of the screen the stick lives on\n- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n- `input.zones = null` †: areas of the screen a finger holds an action down in, [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }] (fractions of the canvas, 0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's two halves, a rhythm game's lanes. A finger landing in one presses act until it lifts (several fingers, several zones), and starts no stick\n\n## 6. Pixel fonts\n    const f = document.activeElement, i = all.indexOf(f), side = dir === 'left' || dir === 'right', d = dir === 'up' || dir === 'left' ? -1 : 1;\n    if (f && side && f.type === 'range') { if (d < 0) f.stepDown(); else f.stepUp(); f.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); return; }\n    if (f && side && f._cycle) { f._cycle(d); return; }\n    const n = all[((i < 0 ? 0 : i + d) + all.length) % all.length]; n.focus({ preventScroll: true }); if (n.scrollIntoView) n.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });\n  }\n}\nE.Shell = Shell;\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 22. GPU LIGHTING (WebGPU)  optional. game.enableGPU({ map }) turns it on.\n *    The Canvas renderer still draws every color. Alongside it, it writes an\n *    \"info\" image (height, surface type, glow per pixel). The GPU then lights each\n *    pixel: colored point lights, soft shadows marched through a heightmap of the\n *    level, light wrapping around characters (normals from their silhouettes),\n *    glow spilling onto nearby surfaces, dithered light bands, and heat shimmer.\n *    If WebGPU is missing or fails, the game keeps the Canvas lighting.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst WGSL_COMMON = /* wgsl */`\nstruct Params {\n  a: vec4f, b: vec4f, c: vec4f, camv: vec4f,\n  right: vec4f, up: vec4f, amb: vec4f, fx: vec4f,\n  mapd: vec4f, scr: vec4f, scr2: vec4f, bufd: vec4f,\n  nheat: vec4f, p0: vec4f, p1: vec4f, p2: vec4f,\n  lights: array<vec4f, 64>,\n  heat: array<vec4f, 8>,\n};\n@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> U: Params;\n@vertex fn vs(@builtin(vertex_index) i: u32) -> @builtin(position) vec4f {\n  var p = array<vec2f, 3>(vec2f(-1.0, -1.0), vec2f(3.0, -1.0), vec2f(-1.0, 3.0));\n  return vec4f(p[i], 0.0, 1.0);\n}\nfn bayer(p: vec2i) -> f32 {\n  var m = array<f32, 16>(0.0, 8.0, 2.0, 10.0, 12.0, 4.0, 14.0, 6.0, 3.0, 11.0, 1.0, 9.0, 15.0, 7.0, 13.0, 5.0);\n  let x = ((p.x % 4) + 4) % 4;\n  let y = ((p.y % 4) + 4) % 4;\n  return (m[y * 4 + x] + 0.5) / 16.0;\n}\n`;\nconst WGSL_LIGHT = /* wgsl */`\n@group(0) @binding(1) var albedoT: texture_2d<f32>;\n@group(0) @binding(2) var infoT: texture_2d<f32>;\n@group(0) @binding(3) var hmT: texture_2d<f32>;\nfn clsOf(v: vec4f) -> i32 { return i32(round(v.g * 12.75)); }\nfn zOf(v: vec4f) -> f32 { return v.r * 85.0; }\nfn hmAt(q: vec2f) -> f32 {\n  let d = vec2i(U.mapd.xy);\n  let t = clamp(vec2i(floor(q * U.fx.w)), vec2i(0, 0), d - vec2i(1, 1));\n  return textureLoad(hmT, t, 0).r * 85.0;\n}\nfn shadowAt(p: vec3f, l: vec3f) -> f32 {\n  let d = l.xy - p.xy;\n  let D = length(d);\n  if (D < 2.0) { return 1.0; }\n  let n = clamp(i32(D * 0.5), 4, 48);\n  let t0 = min(0.9, 4.5 / D);\n  var s = 1.0;\n  for (var k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n    let t = mix(t0, 0.97, (f32(k) + 0.5) / f32(n));\n    let rz = mix(p.z, l.z, t);\n    let h = hmAt(p.xy + d * t);\n    let occ = clamp((h - rz) / (0.8 + t * D * 0.05), 0.0, 1.0);\n    s = min(s, 1.0 - occ);\n    if (s <= 0.0) { break; }\n9363:const SHELL_CSS = `.esh{position:fixed;inset:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:20;font:14px/1.45 var(--font);color:var(--ink);--sat:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);\n9369:.esh-obj{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);top:var(--pt);max-width:min(330px,58vw)}.esh-obj b{font:600 17px var(--title);display:block}\n9371:.esh-vit{text-align:right;min-width:120px}.esh-hb{display:flex;gap:6px;pointer-events:auto}.esh-hb button{padding:6px 10px;font-size:11px;background:var(--paper)}\n9385:@media (pointer:coarse){.esh-keys{display:none}}@media (max-width:640px){.esh-obj{max-width:calc(100vw - 214px)}.esh-toast{left:var(--pl);right:var(--pr);top:auto;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 124px);max-wi [... omitted end of long line]\n9387:.esh-sh{position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#04060acc;pointer-events:auto;padding:calc(var(--pt) + 46px) var(--pr) var(--pb) var(--pl);animation:esh-in .25s;touch-acti [... omitted end of long line]\n9391:.esh-mod{width:min(460px,100%);max-height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:22px 24px}.esh-wide{width:min(760px,100%)}\n9392:.esh-ttl{place-items:center start;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#04060aee,#04060a99 50%,#04060a00 85%)}.esh-ttl>div{max-width:min(520px,92vw);padding-left:4vw}\n9393:.esh-ttl h1{font-size:clamp(44px,10vw,92px);letter-spacing:.07em}.esh-sub{font:italic 20px var(--title);color:var(--accent);margin-top:6px}\n9446:    if (!document.getElementById('esh-css')) { const st = document.createElement('style'); st.id = 'esh-css'; st.textContent = SHELL_CSS; document.head.appendChild(st); }\n9456:    this._els = { hb: E2('esh-hb', col), obj: E2('esh-obj esh-pan'), vit: E2('esh-vit esh-pan', col), place: E2('esh-place', col), tip: E2('esh-tip esh-pan'), pr: E2('esh-pr esh-pan'), keys: E2('esh-k [... omitted end of long line]\n9712:    const sh = this._el('div', 'esh-sh' + (title ? ' esh-ttl' : '')), box = this._el('div', title ? '' : 'esh-pan esh-mod' + (name === 'map' ? ' esh-wide' : ''));\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
