{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'head -25 Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/reports/network-campaign.json && head -20 Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/reports/hub-harness.json && head -15 Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/reports/simulation-tests.json && ls Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/tests && cat Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453/docs/simulation-verification.md | tail -30'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"artifact\": \"Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453.html\",\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"actual delivered file pairs two contexts through production WebRTC\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"remote sub-interval fire uses one real shaft exactly once\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"standard-rules two-ranger expedition reaches shared victory\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"production tools, relics, quiver and wounds agree on both copies\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"every projectile applies at most one wound across real peers\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"contested authored supply credits exactly its seven shafts\",\n{\n  \"artifact\": \"Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453.html\",\n  \"sha256\": \"abb23b279d7361f53a21bd59284cf34e466c19ed49b25929736d049c030408e1\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"scenario\": \"two-player\",\n      \"done\": true,\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"game\": \"/Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453.html\",\n      \"players\": 2,\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"head metas\",\n          \"pass\": true,\n          \"detail\": \"hub:session=1 mode=shared-world\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"hub:session-players is a range within 1\\u20134\",\n          \"pass\": true,\n          \"detail\": \"hub:session-players=1-2\"\n{\n  \"passed\": 49,\n  \"failed\": 0,\n  \"failures\": [],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"all authored content validates\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"27 chambers each have a purposeful encounter or reveal\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tool chain never depends on its own reward\",\naudio-browser.py\nbrowser.py\nextended-browser.py\nnetwork-browser.py\nnetwork-campaign.py\nnetwork-hub.py\nnetwork-lifecycle.py\nnetwork.test.cjs\nproduct.mjs\nrender-browser.py\nrender.test.mjs\nsimulation.mjs\n# Simulation verification\n\nActual run: `node tests/simulation.mjs` → **49 passed, 0 failed**. Details: `reports/simulation-tests.json`.\n\nThe complete expedition is exercised through sequenced production commands inside the real engine’s headless `E.Game.advance()` fixed-step lifecycle. No warps, tool grants, enemy kills, state loads, tuned stats, immortal flags or external ammunition are used. The director obtains all three tools, rings the mandatory bank gong, hits and evades the indestructible ooze, explores the optional caches, defeats the entire damageable roster, exploits the first guardian's flank, waits for each second-guardian recovery cycle, obtains both Crown halves and takes the real ladder to victory.\n\nPerfect-knowledge sprint clear: **140.8583 simulation seconds**, 48 shots, 30 hits, 12 banks, 4 optional treasures, 3 recovered shafts, 0 deaths, 0 restarts, 0 damage, assisted false. This is a deterministic speedrun, not first-time human pacing evidence. Physical controller, human audio listening, mobile hardware, WAN/NAT and 18–25 minute first-play timing remain unverified by this subsystem.\n\n## Defects actually found and fixed\n\n- **SIM-001 · critical**: the authored Root Hollow entry corridor ended four cells before the vertical path, making the rest of the section unreachable. Content reachability validation caught this. Extended the explicit corridor through the junction.\n- **SIM-002 · moderate**: room/reward and cross-wing prop IDs collided. Global stable-ID validation caught this. Renamed the conflicting room IDs and namespaced every compiled prop ID by section.\n- **SIM-003 · moderate**: after adding physical low-bank collision, direct movement steering could aim through the diagonal bank and stall despite a valid route around it. The complete action replay exposed this. Added radius-aware move-clear queries and made navigation use passable cell centers around bank geometry; steering now routes around blockers.\n\nTwo test-only driver defects were also fixed: center-point firing clearance at a wall corner, and one undefined test constant. These are not counted as shipped gameplay defects. The most helpful test was the complete command expedition plus authored graph validation: it exposed actual progression blockers. The least helpful exploratory run was a long replay allowed to continue after a repeated stuck position; the focused reproduction gave the same result much faster.\n\n## Known practical bounds\n\nSnapshot JSON measured under the Hub's 16KB cap in the complete replay; checkpoint/history is never sent with each dynamic snapshot. Engine lifecycle supplies the one fixed simulation clock. Gameplay drawing consumes no simulation randomness or state. Authority/source transport checks are performed by the application/network owners in separate suites.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
