{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_125","type":"agent_message","text":"Built [**Dungeons and Deeper Trouble**](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-035453__x2713fa/work/Dungeons-and-Deeper-Trouble-Advanced-Dungeons-and-Dragons-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-035453.html).\n\nThe single HTML includes 27 chambers, both guardians, co-op, saves, controller/touch controls, developer tools and attract mode. **310 distinct checks passed; zero failures.**\n\n[Interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-035453__x2713fa/work/exit-interview.json) · [Progress](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-035453__x2713fa/work/PROGRESS.md)\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-06 03:54:53. Source: [Advanced Dungeons & Dragons, 1982](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/addcloudy.html). Plan: PLAN.md.\n\n- Genre/perspective: action adventure, overhead three-quarter.\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 0.89.1, Hub client 1.4.0, JavaScript, Canvas, Web Audio and WebRTC.\n- Art/animation: original native shaded pixel art, extended humanoid rigs and procedural creatures.\n- Audio: synthesized music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%.\n- Online: solo, couch co-op, direct WebRTC and Hub shared-world.\n- Testing/research: headless playthroughs, browser/input/audio/network checks and visual review; original manual, history, screenshot, engine, Hub and WebRTC documentation inspected.\n- Environment/model: Codex CLI headless Linux; OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, ultra. Usage: **added on import**.\n- Real hardware, human listening, WAN compatibility and first-play timing: **unknown**.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** Testing found 12 defects, including four game-breaking defects; all were fixed. Full campaign and departure replays were most useful. Continuing an already-stuck replay was least useful.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Best: native rigs and fixed stepping. Wrong turns: title-camera and audio lifecycle handling. Largest addition: authoritative expedition simulation. Hardest: projection, visibility and synchronization. Engine changes: none; game extensions only. Suggested improvement: executable bow/shared-world examples.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Best: concrete mechanics and acceptance gates. Unclear: verifying first-play duration without human testing. Hardest: consistent behavior across every play mode. Suggested improvement: an executable integration fixture and human pacing review."}}
